{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Headwire"}],"role":"article","title":"Features and the input path"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppFeature","doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppView"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The app keeps two kinds of work apart. Every decision a person can see, such as which capture card is open, which path carries video and which carries input, or whether the settings sheet is up, is state in a reducer and is tested with a ","type":"text"},{"code":"TestStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Work that happens per frame, per input event, or per audio sample never goes through the store: reducers start it, configure it, and switch it, and it runs on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-feature-tree","level":2,"text":"The feature tree"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/AppFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":" is the root and the one screen. It scopes these child features:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/StreamFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps the capture session pointed at the right device and reports what the stream is doing, including the card’s status and the rectangle the Mac’s picture is drawn in.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps each video and input path’s health, asks ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/PathSelector","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the live pair, and decides when a backup stream runs. It publishes the result as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityStatus","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SoundFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" plays the Mac’s sound from whichever video is shown.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MacDisplayFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" asks the helper to mirror the Mac or extend it onto this screen while the helper’s stream is shown.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/HelperPairingFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" asks before the helper link pairs over the Bluetooth bond.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/BluetoothHostFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" decides which Bluetooth host gets the keyboard and pointer: a paired Mac its helper names, or the one the person chooses.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/UntypedTextFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" names the characters Bluetooth couldn’t type.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SettingsFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":" is presented as the settings sheet and scopes ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectionSettingsFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/CardProfilesFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/SoundSettingsFeature","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The root forwards changes between siblings. When the stream’s card status changes, connectivity hears of it. When connectivity changes the shown video, the stream and the Mac display feature hear of it. When the picture’s rectangle changes, the input path is told the size the Mac’s picture is drawn at.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"From-a-touch-to-the-Mac","level":2,"text":"From a touch to the Mac"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurface","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" puts an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSurfaceUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" over the video. The view is first responder while input is active, so it receives touches, Pencil, pointer, and hardware key presses. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/MouseInput","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" feeds GameController mouse motion and buttons, which report raw relative motion even while the pointer is locked.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each surface’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRouter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" turns that input into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InputEvent"},{"text":" values in arrival order. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TouchInputMapper","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" maps gestures for the pointer mode in effect, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/KeyboardTracker","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps each key down at most once, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ButtonMerger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" merges a click that arrives from both GameController and UIKit into one press. Every router and the mouse share one serial queue, so the main thread’s load can’t delay mouse events and there is a single order across all of them.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The router hands each event to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which delivers it through the one ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputDelivery","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Delivery shapes every event with the person’s pointer speed and scroll direction, then passes it to the active input sink: the Bluetooth HID sink, or the helper link’s sink on one transport.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/ConnectivityFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" decides which path is active. To switch, it takes the new path’s sink from ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputSinksClient","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and calls ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switchTo"},{"text":". Delivery releases every key and button on the old sink and waits for that, for at most 150 ms, before the new sink hears anything. The new sink first hears a key-down for each modifier key still held, so a ⌘ held through the switch still makes the next C a copy, and then the events that arrived meanwhile, replayed in order, except the ups for keys and buttons the release already covered. Other keys still held are not pressed again, since they would auto-repeat on the Mac.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The on-screen keyboard takes a different route into the same router. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TextEntryView","type":"reference"},{"text":" reports each edit as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/TextEdit","type":"reference"},{"text":", the backspaces and new text the Mac must see, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/HardwareKeyForwarding","type":"reference"},{"text":" says which hardware keys go to the Mac while that view is first responder. The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/KeyRow","type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s keys, for the keys iPadOS won’t pass to an app, are submitted through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Headwire\/InputRoutingClient","type":"reference"},{"text":" so they keep their place among the surfaces’ events.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the app’s reducers fit together, and how a touch or a key press reaches the Mac without passing through them."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/headwire\/featuresandinput"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.nth.headwire\/documentation\/Hea